    {
      "id": "p0005-b003",
      "kind": "text",
      "bbox": [
        54.0,
        162.0,
        299.0,
        232.0
      ],
      "markdown": "We leverage Lemma 1 to verify different properties of a given cell _Br_ ( _·_ ). In particular, Theorem 4 below gives us a condition that verifies whether a cell _Br_ ( _x_ ) is completely inside _Rτ_ ( _Xu_ ), completely outside _Rτ_ ( _Xu_ ), or partially inside _Rτ_ ( _Xu_ ). This will be critical to over approximate _Rτ_ ( _Xu_ ).",
      "source_class": "text"
    },
    {
      "id": "p0005-b004",
      "kind": "text",
      "bbox": [
        53.0,
        239.0,
        299.0,
        262.0
      ],
      "markdown": "**Theorem 4.** _Consider a state x ∈X , and let Br_ ( _x_ ) := _{y|∥y − x∥≤ r} be a neighborhood of x. Then, we have:_",
